! WJP: ac7h13f is c7h13-1-2 in Mani's iso-alkane mech. c7h13-1-2 is a lumped species.  Radical site is not specified.   
! Since it is lumped it has many beta scisson paths.  Here, since we know the radical site location, it has only
! one main path.  If we want to unlump, do we call it c7h13-1-2f? But this would cause complications is a surrogate mech.  
! On the other hand, these radicals
! can isomerize, so we probably need to keep them for now so that we can account for isomerization.
!
