!5 member 
! EJS july 07: Direct elimination of HO2 and olefin from ro2 added:                                     
MCH2OO=MCH2ENE+HO2 5.65E+04 2.5 27397. ! Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => cychexene+ho2, 50 bar rate ! a-factor /2 - for consistency with chx 
!mch2oo=mch1ene+ho2 5.65E+04 2.5 27397. ! Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => cychexene+ho2, 50 bar rate ! a-factor /2 - for consistency with chx
MCH2OO=MCH1ENE+HO2 5.65E+03 2.5 27397. ! Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => cychexene+ho2, 50 bar rate 
                                             ! a-factor /2 - for consistency with chx
                                             ! WJP: Reduced further by a factor of 10 because HO2 elimination can only occur if the -OO and the -H
                                             ! are in the same plane (MM).  This only occurs if the methyl group is in the equalateral position
                                             ! which is not the lowest energy conformer.
!mch2oo=mch2ene+ho2 3.85E+12 0. 29000. ! Ranzi et al (2006) ! a-factor /2 - for consistency with chx 
!mch2oo=mch1ene+ho2 3.85E+12 0. 29000. ! Ranzi et al (2006) ! a-factor /2 - for consistency with chx 
!                                                                                                       
!mch2oo=mch2qj3    1.0E+13   0.0   26850. !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, A-factor adjusted for # of rotors
!mch2oo=mch2qj3    2.00E+11 0. 29350.0 !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, sec C-H, Ea+2.5kcal from Gulati and Walker.
MCH2OO=MCH2QJ3    5.6E-05 4.9 24191.0 !Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q2j, 50 bar rate ! a-factor /2 - for consistency with chx.
!mch2oo=mch2qj3    1.2E+11 0.0 27500.0 !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, sec C-H, A-factor times 0.6, Ea+0.6kcal from Handford-Styring and Walker.
!mch2oo=mch2qj1    5.0E+12   0.0   24100. !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, A-factor adjusted for # of rotors
!mch2oo=mch2qj1   1.00E+11 0.0 26600.0 !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, sec C-H, Ea+2.5kcal from Gulati and Walker
!mch2oo=mch2qj1    6.2e10 0.0 24700.0 !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, tert C-H, A-factor times 0.6, Ea+0.6kcal from Handford-Styring and Walker.
MCH2OO=MCH2QJ1    5.6E-05 4.9 24191.0 !Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q2j, 50 bar rate ! 
                                        !Divide A-factor by 2 compared to chx. Rate is slower because the most favorable position is when
                                        !OO is axial and the H being pulled off is equilateral.
                                        !However, rate is faster because C-H is tertiary.  Assume this factor of 2 effect cancels out.
!mch2qj3=mchyo23+oh    6.3E+12   0.0   15900. ! Green et al. JPCA 2003; Adjusted A-factors for # of rotors.
MCH2QJ3=MCHYO23+OH    8.61E+14 -0.7 13133.0  ! Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chx1q2j => chxyo12+oh, 50 bar rate
!WJP, 2012-02-10: unlump mche
MCH2ENE+HO2=MCH2QJ3    8.0E+10   0.0   7000.    ! CVN: HO2 addition to double bond.
!mche+ho2=mch2qj3    8.0E+10   0.0   7000.    ! CVN: HO2 addition to double bond.
!mch1ene+ho2=mch2qj1    8.0E+10   0.0   7000.  ! CVN: HO2 addition to double bond.
MCH2QJ1=MCH1ENE+HO2   3.48E+23 -3.2 21603.0  ! Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chx1q2j => cychexene+ho2, 50 bar rate 
MCH2QJ1=MCHYO23+OH    8.61E+14 -0.7 13133.0  ! Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chx1q2j => chxyo12+oh, 50 bar rate
!mche+ho2=mch2qj1    8.0E+10   0.0   7000.  ! CVN: HO2 addition to double bond.
!6 member h transfer
! factor of 48 for one rotor not tied up:
!mch2oo=mch2qx     1.8E+12   0.0   24400.  !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, A-factor adjusted for # of rotors
!mch2oo=mch2qx     2.25e11   0.0   24400.  !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, A-factor adjusted for # of rotors
!mch2oo=mch2qx     1.1e11   0.0   24400.  !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, A-factor adjusted by 3 for # of rotors
                                            
!mch2oo=mch2qx     1.1e11   0.0   16500.  !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, A-factor adjusted by 3 for # of rotors
                                            !Reduce Ea for abstraction by 7.6 kcal from methyl group compared to abstracting 
                                            ! from a ring CH2 group, according Yang et al. CF2010 (WJP):
!mch2oo=mch2qx     8.4E-03 4.9 27191.0  !Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q2j, 50 bar rate ! a-factor x 3/4 - for consistency with chx.
                                         ! Add 3 kcal for primary C-H instead of secondary (ave of diff in bond strength and Ea's from HO2+alkanes
MCH2OO=MCH2QX     1.92E6     1.82  19720.0  !Davis and Pitz, ab intio rate with tunneling and rotor calculations 12/2012
!mch2oo=mch2qj4     2.5E+10   0.0   23350. !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, sec C-H, Ea+2.5kcal from Gulati and Walker
!mch2oo=mch2qj4     9.3E+10   0.0   24100. !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, sec C-H, A-factor times 3.7 & Ea+3.2kcal 
                                            ! from Handford-String and Walker
MCH2OO=MCH2QJ4     2.83E+02 2.7 21637.0 !Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q3j, 50 bar rate ! a-factor/2 - for consistency with chx. 
!mch2oo=mch2qj6     2.0E+13   0.0   20850. !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, A-factor adjusted for # of rotors
!mch2oo=mch2qj6     2.5E+10   0.0   23350. !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, sec C-H, Ea+2.5kcal from Gulati and Walker
!mch2oo=mch2qj6     9.3E+10   0.0   24100. !Curran et al. Isooctane, CF2002, sec C-H, A-factor times 3.7 & Ea+3.2kcal 
                                            ! from Handford-String and Walker
MCH2OO=MCH2QJ6     2.83E+02 2.7 21637.0 !Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q3j, 50 bar rate ! a-factor/2 - for consistency with chx. 
MCH2QX=CHXYCO-2+OH    9.1E+12   0.0   21900.  !chxyco-2 is a cyclic ether with a 4 membered ring: 
                                                ! the o attaches to the ch2 group and the 2 position on the ring
! radical site on CH2 group abstracts H atom from carbon no. 2 with OOH group:
MCH2QX=MCHO+OH     1.5E+13   0.0   35000.  ! CVN: assumed the same as alkyl isomerization.  Adjusted for C-H bond strength. mcho is a lumped species
                                             ! with a carbonyl group.  (does not contribute at 800K, 45 atm)
!mch2qj4=mchyo24+oh    4.0E+12   0.0   19500.    !mchyo24 is a lumped cyclic oxide with 4-mem CCCO ring on MCH
MCH2QJ4=C7ENE-ONE+OH   2.28E+09 0.8 17616.0 ! Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chx1q3j => hex5enal+oh, 50 bar rate ! 
                                              ! 1,3 epoxide is unstable and quickly decomposes to C7ene-al (a lumped species) (Gulati and Walker 1989)
                                              ! However, Lille observes the 1,3epoxide in the RCM. 
DUP
!mch2qj6=mchyo24+oh    4.0E+12   0.0   19500.    !mchyo24 is a lumped cyclic oxide with 4-mem CCCO ring on MCH
MCH2QJ6=C7ENE-ONE+OH   2.28E+09 0.8 17616.0 ! Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chx1q3j => hex5enal+oh, 50 bar rate ! 
                                              ! 1,3 epoxide is unstable and quickly decomposes to C7ene-al (a lumped species) (Gulati and Walker 1989)
                                              ! However, Lille observes the 1,3epoxide in the RCM. 
DUP
! further decomposition paths for gamma mchXqjY
! gamma mchXqjY radical means OOH group is "gamma" to the radical site
! (add these for all gamma mchXqjY if important)=> They are important: 5 times faster at 800K than cyclic ether formation!
! Use to calculate decomposition rate of gamma radical mch2qj4:(mchj2q4ene is c*cccc(c)cjooh):
! mchj2q4ene=mch2qj4   1.00E+08 0.86 5.900E+03 ! A-factor and n from Matheu et al. IJCK 2003 for 1,6 addition to terminal c*c.
!mch2qj6=oh+c7ene-one 7.62e16 -0.43 27904.2 ! calculated from reverse rate of mchj2q4ene=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
MCH2QJ6 => OH+C7ENE-ONE 3.8E16 -0.43 27904.2 ! calculated from reverse rate of mchj2q4ene=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
                                               ! Product decomposes rapidly to c7ene-al+OH.  Irrevisible since overall reaction
!
DUP
!mch2qj4=oh+c7ene-one 7.62e16 -0.43 27904.2 ! calculated from reverse rate of mchj2q4ene=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
MCH2QJ4 => OH+C7ENE-ONE 3.8E16 -0.43 27904.2 ! calculated from reverse rate of mchj2q4ene=mch2qj4 using ChemRev (species to calculate gamma scission of mch2qj4)
                                               ! Product decomposes rapidly to c7ene-al+OH.  Irrevisible since overall reaction
DUP
!mch2qx=oh+c7ene-one 7.62e16 -0.43 27904.2 ! calculated from reverse rate of mchj2q4ene=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
MCH2QX => OH+C7ENE-ONE 3.8E16 -0.43 27904.2 ! calculated from reverse rate of mchj2q4ene=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
                                               ! Product decomposes rapidly to c7ene-al+OH.  Irrevisible since overall reaction
C7ENE-ONE+OH =C7ENE-ONEJ+H2O  2.00E+06 1.8   1300.0  ! Analogy with ch3cho+oh, Taylor et al. Proc. Comb. Symp., 26, p. 497-504 (1996)
C7ENE-ONE+HO2=C7ENE-ONEJ+H2O2 4.82E+03 2.6   13910.0 ! Analogy with ch3cho+ho2, from Curran et al. 2004, C3_31 mech
C7ENE-ONE+H  =C7ENE-ONEJ+H2   1.34E+13 0.0   3300.0  ! Assume rate rule for aldehydic H from nc7_38 LLNL mech 
!                                                            (ch3cho+h from Whytock et al. J. Chem. Phys. 65 (1976).
C7ENE-ONE+CH3=C7ENE-ONEJ+CH4  1.34E+13 0.0   3300.0  ! Assume rate rule for aldehydic H from nc7_38 LLNL mech
