                                                ! From NIST database, Radom et al
                                                ! Can J. Chem 81: 431-442 (2003)                
X3C6H11CHO-27=MCH2N1OJ 1.00E+08 0.86 1903. ! Beta route leading to ring opening
                                             ! Matheu et al. Table 1 IJCK  35: 95�119 (2003) for 1,6 exo addition
                                             ! as used to determine MCH Orme paper Table 10 JPCA vol 110. 114-131 (2006)
C2H4+AC3H4COCH3=X3C6H11CHO-27  8.5E+10 0.0 11300. ! add. of 'allyls type rad' (c=ccjc(=o)c) to terminal c of c=c
                                                      ! analogy with addition of allylic rad to terminal c in c=c-c
                                                      ! Sumathi CBS-Q, cited in Matheu et al. IJCK 35: 95-110 (2003)           
JC6H10CHO-LG=MCH2N4OJ 1.00E+08 0.86 1903. ! Beta route leading to ring opening
                                            ! Matheu et al. Table 1 IJCK  35: 95�119 (2003) for 1,6 exo addition 
                                            ! as used to determine MCH Orme paper Table 10 JPCA vol 110. 114-131 (2006)
C2H4+AC3H4CH2CHO=JC6H10CHO-LG 8.5E+10 0.0 11300. ! add. of allyls type rad. to c of c=c
                                                     ! analogy with addition of allylic rad to terminal c in c=c-c
                                                     ! Sumathi CBS-Q, cited in Matheu et al. IJCK 35: 95-110 (2003)             
X2C6H10CHO-16=MCH3N2OJ 1.00E+08 0.86 1903. ! Beta route leading to ring opening
                                            ! Matheu et al. Table 1 IJCK  35: 95�119 (2003) for 1,6 exo addition
                                            ! as used to determine MCH Orme paper Table 10 JPCA vol 110. 114-131 (2006)
C3H6+CH2CHCHCHO=X2C6H10CHO-16 8.5E+10 0.0 11300. ! add. of allyls type radical to terminal c of c=c 
                                                   ! analogy with addition of allylic rad to terminal c in c=c-c
                                                   ! Sumathi CBS-Q, cited in Matheu et al. IJCK 35: 95-110 (2003)            
DC6H10CHO-FA=MCH3N5OJ 1.00E+08 0.86 1903. ! Beta route leading to ring opening
                                            ! Matheu et al. Table 1 IJCK  35: 95�119 (2003) for 1,6 endo addition 
                                            !(WJP: no exo addition rate in table.  Looks like Ea was reduced by 4 kcal for exo 
                                            ! rather than endo addition. Seems like Ea should be increased for exo addition)
                                            ! as used to determine MCH Orme paper Table 10 JPCA vol 110. 114-131 (2006)
C3H6+CH2CHCHCHO=DC6H10CHO-FA 8.5E+10 0.0 11300. ! add. of allyls type radical to internal c of c=c
                                                   ! analogy with addition of allylic rad to terminal c in c=c-c
                                                   ! Sumathi CBS-Q, cited in Matheu et al. IJCK 35: 95-110 (2003)             
HX2*CH21*O6J=CHXDCH22OJ 1.00E+08 0.86 1903. ! Beta route leading to ring opening
                                              ! Matheu et al. Table 1 IJCK  35: 95�119 (2003) for 1,6 exo addition
                                              ! as used to determine MCH Orme paper Table 10 JPCA vol 110. 114-131 (2006)
C2H4+C4H6CHO1-24=HX2*CH21*O6J 1.32E+4 2.48 6130. ! add. of 'c2h5' rad. to terminal c of c=c
                                                      ! analogy with c2h4+c2h5=pc4h9, Table 3 from H.J. Curran 
                                                      ! Int J Chem Kinet 38:250�275, (2006)            
!C2H4+C3H3O=C4H6CHO1-24 2.00E+11 0.0 2010.0 ! add. of 'vins' type rad to terminal c of c=c 
                                                  ! Analogy with c2h4+c2h3 from Weissman and Benson IJCK (1989), 
                                                  ! Benson says Ea is lower limit                 
