!
! Reaction Class 5: H-atom abstraction reactions from alkenes
!
! Consider products based on abstraction of allylic sites, but increase abstraction rate to account 
! for abstraction from all possible sites.
! For non-allylic sites, increase number of allylic sites used to compute A-factor by one 
! for each ch2 group or ch3 group.
! Use secondary allylic rate constants from Mehl 11/14/2013 from gasoline surrogate mechanism.
!
! nbch-1ene:
! 3 allylic sites for abstraction:
!
! CHECK !!!! We consume nbch-1n6j later.
! 2 secondary allylic Hs, one secondary ch2 group on ring => degeneracy=3
!
NBCH-1ENE+O2    => NBCH-1N3J+HO2    3.30E+12 0.0 3.72E+04 
NBCH-1ENE+OH    => NBCH-1N3J+H2O    4.14E+04 2.64 -1919.0 
NBCH-1ENE+H     => NBCH-1N3J+H2     5.06E+05 2.36 2.07E+02
NBCH-1ENE+O     => NBCH-1N3J+OH     9.90E+05 2.43 1.21E+03
NBCH-1ENE+HO2   => NBCH-1N3J+H2O2   1.45E+04 2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-1ENE+CH3   => NBCH-1N3J+CH4    5.54E+00 3.31 4.00E+03
NBCH-1ENE+CH3O2 => NBCH-1N3J+CH3O2H 7.23+03  2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-1ENE+CH3O  => NBCH-1N3J+CH3OH  6.00E+01 2.90 8.61E+03
!
!
! 2 secondary allylic Hs, one secondary ch2 group on ring => degeneracy=3
!
NBCH-1ENE+O2    => NBCH-1N6J+HO2    3.30E+12 0.0 3.72E+04 
NBCH-1ENE+OH    => NBCH-1N6J+H2O    4.14E+04 2.64 -1919.0 
NBCH-1ENE+H     => NBCH-1N6J+H2     5.06E+05 2.36 2.07E+02
NBCH-1ENE+O     => NBCH-1N6J+OH     9.90E+05 2.43 1.21E+03
NBCH-1ENE+HO2   => NBCH-1N6J+H2O2   1.45E+04 2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-1ENE+CH3   => NBCH-1N6J+CH4    5.54E+00 3.31 4.00E+03
NBCH-1ENE+CH3O2 => NBCH-1N6J+CH3O2H 7.23+03 2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-1ENE+CH3O  => NBCH-1N6J+CH3OH  6.00E+01 2.90 8.61E+03
!
! 2 secondary allylic Hs.  Also consider 2 secondary CH2s and 1 CH3 on alkyl side group => deg=5
! Product species same as nbch-an-2j since are resonant structures
!
NBCH-1ENE+O2    => NBCH-1N-AJ+HO2    5.500E+12 0.0 3.72E+04   
NBCH-1ENE+OH    => NBCH-1N-AJ+H2O    6.91E4    2.64 -1919.0
NBCH-1ENE+H     => NBCH-1N-AJ+H2     8.440E+05 2.36 2.07E+02  
NBCH-1ENE+O     => NBCH-1N-AJ+OH     1.650E+06 2.43 1.21E+03  
NBCH-1ENE+HO2   => NBCH-1N-AJ+H2O2   2.410E+04 2.55 1.05E+04  
NBCH-1ENE+CH3   => NBCH-1N-AJ+CH4    9.22E+00  3.31 4.00E+03  
NBCH-1ENE+CH3O2 => NBCH-1N-AJ+CH3O2H 1.21E+04  2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-1ENE+CH3O  => NBCH-1N-AJ+CH3OH  1.00E+02  2.90 8.61E+03
!
! nbch-2ene:
!
! 1 tertiary allylic H.  Also consider 3 secondary CH2s and 1 CH3 on alkyl side group => deg=5
! nbch2n1j is resonant with nbch-1n3j
! Since a tertiary C-H is only 0.5 kcal weaker that secondary allylic C-H, use secondary allylic rates,
! except for RH+HO2 where the tertiary allylic rate is available.
!
