!
! 1 tertiary allylic H.  Also consider 5 secondary CH2s ring => deg=6
! nbch-bn-1j is resonant with nbch-an-bj
! Since a tertiary C-H is only 0.5 kcal weaker that secondary allylic C-H, use secondary allylic rates,
! except for RH+HO2 where tertiary allylic rates are available.
!
NBCH-B-ENE+O2    => NBCH-AN-BJ+HO2    6.60E+12 0.0 3.72E+04
NBCH-B-ENE+OH    => NBCH-AN-BJ+H2O    8.29E+04 2.64 -1919.0
NBCH-B-ENE+H     => NBCH-AN-BJ+H2     1.01E+06 2.36 2.07E+02
NBCH-B-ENE+O     => NBCH-AN-BJ+OH     1.89E+06 2.43 1.21E+03
NBCH-B-ENE+HO2   => NBCH-AN-BJ+H2O2   2.04E+04 2.50 8.92E+03 ! Scott & Walker CnF2002, estimate
NBCH-B-ENE+CH3   => NBCH-AN-BJ+CH4    1.11E+01 3.31 4.00E+03
NBCH-B-ENE+CH3O2 => NBCH-AN-BJ+CH3O2H 1.45E+04 2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-B-ENE+CH3O  => NBCH-AN-BJ+CH3OH  1.20E2   2.90 8.61E+03
!
! 2 secondary allylic Hs.  Also consider 1 primary CH3 => deg=3
! nbch-bn-1j is resonant with nbch-an-bj
!
NBCH-B-ENE+O2    => NBCH-BN-CJ+HO2    3.30E+12 0.0 3.72E+04 
NBCH-B-ENE+OH    => NBCH-BN-CJ+H2O    4.14E+04 2.64 -1919.0 
NBCH-B-ENE+H     => NBCH-BN-CJ+H2     5.06E+05 2.36 2.07E+02
NBCH-B-ENE+O     => NBCH-BN-CJ+OH     9.90E+05 2.43 1.21E+03
NBCH-B-ENE+HO2   => NBCH-BN-CJ+H2O2   1.45E+04 2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-B-ENE+CH3   => NBCH-BN-CJ+CH4    5.53E+00 3.31 4.00E+03
NBCH-B-ENE+CH3O2 => NBCH-BN-CJ+CH3O2H 7.23E+03 2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-B-ENE+CH3O  => NBCH-BN-CJ+CH3OH  6.00E+01 2.90 8.61E+03
!
! nbch-c-ene
!
! 2 secondary allylic sites, plus 5 ch2 sites and one tertiary site (count as 1/2), => deg= 7.5
! (nbch-cn-aj is resonant with nbch-bn-cj
!
NBCH-C-ENE+O2    => NBCH-BN-CJ+HO2    8.25E+12 0.0 3.72E+04
NBCH-C-ENE+OH    => NBCH-BN-CJ+H2O    1.04E5   2.64 -1919.0
NBCH-C-ENE+H     => NBCH-BN-CJ+H2     1.27E+06 2.36 2.07E+02
NBCH-C-ENE+O     => NBCH-BN-CJ+OH     2.48E+06 2.43 1.21E+03
NBCH-C-ENE+HO2   => NBCH-BN-CJ+H2O2   3.62E+04 2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-C-ENE+CH3   => NBCH-BN-CJ+CH4    1.38E+01 3.31 4.00E+03
NBCH-C-ENE+CH3O2 => NBCH-BN-CJ+CH3O2H 1.81E+04 2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-C-ENE+CH3O  => NBCH-BN-CJ+CH3OH  1.50E+02 2.90 8.61E+03
!
! 3 primary allylic sites => deg=3
! (nbch-cn-aj is resonant with nbch-bn-cj
!
NBCH-C-ENE+O2    => NBCH-CN-DJ+HO2    5.50E+12  0.00  3.990E+04
NBCH-C-ENE+OH    => NBCH-CN-DJ+H2O    3.12E+06  2.00  -1.298E+03
NBCH-C-ENE+H     => NBCH-CN-DJ+H2     1.73E+05  2.50  2.492E+03
NBCH-C-ENE+O     => NBCH-CN-DJ+OH     4.41E+05  2.42  3.150E+03
NBCH-C-ENE+HO2   => NBCH-CN-DJ+H2O2   2.70E+04  2.50  1.234E+04
NBCH-C-ENE+CH3   => NBCH-CN-DJ+CH4    2.21E+00  3.50  5.675E+03
NBCH-C-ENE+CH3O2 => NBCH-CN-DJ+CH3O2H 9.64E+03  2.60  1.391E+04
NBCH-C-ENE+CH3O  => NBCH-CN-DJ+CH3OH  9.00E+01  2.95  1.199E+04
!
! nbch-d-ene
!
! 2 secondary allylic sites, plus 6 ch2 sites and one tertiary site (count as 1/2), => deg= 8.5
! (nbch-dn-bj is resonant with nbch-cn-dj
!
NBCH-D-ENE+O2    => NBCH-CN-DJ+HO2    9.35E+12 0.0 3.72E+04
NBCH-D-ENE+OH    => NBCH-CN-DJ+H2O    1.17E5   2.64 -1919.0
NBCH-D-ENE+H     => NBCH-CN-DJ+H2     1.43E+06 2.36 2.07E+02
NBCH-D-ENE+O     => NBCH-CN-DJ+OH     2.81E+06 2.43 1.21E+03
NBCH-D-ENE+HO2   => NBCH-CN-DJ+H2O2   4.10E+04 2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-D-ENE+CH3   => NBCH-CN-DJ+CH4    1.57E+01 3.31 4.00E+03
NBCH-D-ENE+CH3O2 => NBCH-CN-DJ+CH3O2H 2.05E+04 2.55 1.05E+04
NBCH-D-ENE+CH3O  => NBCH-CN-DJ+CH3OH  1.70E+02 2.90 8.61E+03
!
! Reaction Class 6: Addition of radical species O and OH to alkenes
!
! Waddington: Addition of OH to double bond
!
! Use rates from Mehl 11/14/2013 from gasoline surrogate mechanism 
! for addition to a double bond with one carbon substitution.
! Consider one set of final products
!
! (In this case, one end of the double bond has 2 carbon substitutions):
NBCH-1ENE+OH=NBCH-1J-2OH 1.00E13 0.0 0.0
NBCH-1J-2OH+O2=NBCH-1OO-2OH 7.50E12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-1OO-2OH=CHX1*O2Q+PC4H9 1.00E12 0.0 2.780E4
!
! addition to either side of double bond can lead to same products:
NBCH-2ENE+OH=NBCH-2J-3OH 1.00E13 0.0 0.0
NBCH-2J-3OH+O2=NBCH-2OO-3OH 7.50E12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-2OO-3OH=C2H4+C6H12-1+CHOCHO+OH 1.00E12 0.0 2.780E4
!
! addition to either side of double bond can lead to same products:
NBCH-3ENE+OH=NBCH-3J-4OH 1.00E13 0.0 0.0
NBCH-3J-4OH+O2=NBCH-3OO-4OH 7.50E12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-3OO-4OH=C2H4+C6H12-1+CHOCHO+OH 1.00E12 0.0 2.780E4
!
NBCH-A-ENE+OH=NBCH-1OH-AJ 1.00E13 0.0 0.0
NBCH-1OH-AJ+O2=NBCH-1OH-AOO 7.50E12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-1OH-AOO=CHX1*O+OH+NC3H7CHO 1.00E12 0.0 2.780E4
!
NBCH-B-ENE+OH=NBCH-AOH-BJ 1.00E13 0.0 0.0
NBCH-AOH-BJ+O2=NBCH-AOH-BOO 7.50E12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-AOH-BOO=CHXRAD+NC4KET12 1.00E12 0.0 2.780E4
!
NBCH-C-ENE+OH=NBCH-BOH-CJ 1.00E13 0.0 0.0
NBCH-BOH-CJ+O2=NBCH-BOH-COO 7.50E12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-BOH-COO=MCHR1+C3KET12 1.00E12 0.0 2.780E4
!
! Addition to a terminal double bond:
! use same products as nbch-c-ene+oh to avoid new product species c2ket12
NBCH-D-ENE+OH=NBCH-COH-DJ 1.00E13 0.0 0.0
NBCH-COH-DJ+O2=NBCH-COH-DOO 6.00E12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-COH-DOO=MCHR1+C3KET12 1.00E12 0.0 2.780E4
!
! Addition of O to double bond:
!
! Rate constant (1.000e+11 0.00 -1.050e+03) from Sarathy et al. 2011, 
! Allocate 1/2 the rate to each side of the double bond
!
! These reaction products will likely ring open and make C10-en-als not in the mechanism.
! Use products arbitrarily assigned from the a - d nbch-enes instead:
!
NBCH-1ENE+O=CHXRAD+CO+NC3H7 1.000E+11 0.00 -1.050E+03 
!
NBCH-2ENE+O=C2H5CO+CYCHEXCH2  1.000E+11 0.00 -1.050E+03 
!
NBCH-3ENE+O=ECH-BJ+CH3CO     1.000E+11 0.00 -1.050E+03
 
! Selection of products guided by Savee et al. PCCP 2012:
!
NBCH-A-ENE+O= CHXRAD+CO+NC3H7 1.000E+11 0.00 -1.050E+03 
!
NBCH-B-ENE+O=C2H5CO+CYCHEXCH2    5.000E+10 0.00 -1.050E+03 
NBCH-B-ENE+O=CHXRAD+CH2CO+C2H5 5.000E+10 0.00 -1.050E+03  
!
NBCH-C-ENE+O=CH3+CH2CO+CYCHEXCH2 5.000E+10 0.00 -1.050E+03 
NBCH-C-ENE+O=ECH-BJ+CH3CO           5.000E+10 0.00 -1.050E+03 
!
NBCH-D-ENE+O= NPCH-CJ+HCO   1.000E+11 0.00 -1.050E+03 
NBCH-D-ENE+O= ECH-BJ+CH2CHO 1.000E+11 0.00 -1.050E+03 
!
!
! Reaction Class 7: Reactions of alkenyl radicals with HO2, CH3O2, and C2H5O2
! (only resonantly stabilized alkenyl radicals since only these are considered in the n-butylcyclohexene mechanism)
! Rate constants reported in Mehl et al. Proc Combust Instit., Supp data 4:
! (close to rate constant used for c3h5-a+ho2)
! Each alkenyl resonantly stabilized radical forms two types of alkenyloxy radicals. They are lumped into one radical here. 
!
NBCH-1N3J  +HO2=NBCH1N3OJ  +OH 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-1N6J  +HO2=NBCH1N6OJ  +OH 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-1N-AJ +HO2=NBCH1N-AOJ +OH 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-2N4J  +HO2=NBCH2N4OJ  +OH 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-3N5J  +HO2=NBCH3N5OJ  +OH 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-AN-BJ+HO2=NBCH-AN-BOJ+OH 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-BN-CJ+HO2=NBCH-BN-COJ+OH 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-CN-DJ+HO2=NBCH-CN-DOJ+OH 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
!
!
NBCH-1N3J  +CH3O2=NBCH1N3OJ   +CH3O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-1N6J  +CH3O2=NBCH1N6OJ   +CH3O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-1N-AJ +CH3O2=NBCH1N-AOJ +CH3O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-2N4J  +CH3O2=NBCH2N4OJ   +CH3O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-3N5J  +CH3O2=NBCH3N5OJ   +CH3O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-AN-BJ+CH3O2=NBCH-AN-BOJ+CH3O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-BN-CJ+CH3O2=NBCH-BN-COJ+CH3O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-CN-DJ+CH3O2=NBCH-CN-DOJ+CH3O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
!
NBCH-1N3J  +C2H5O2=NBCH1N3OJ   +C2H5O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-1N6J  +C2H5O2=NBCH1N6OJ   +C2H5O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-1N-AJ +C2H5O2=NBCH1N-AOJ +C2H5O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-2N4J  +C2H5O2=NBCH2N4OJ   +C2H5O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-3N5J  +C2H5O2=NBCH3N5OJ   +C2H5O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-AN-BJ+C2H5O2=NBCH-AN-BOJ+C2H5O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-BN-CJ+C2H5O2=NBCH-BN-COJ+C2H5O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
NBCH-CN-DJ+C2H5O2=NBCH-CN-DOJ+C2H5O 9.64E+12 0.0 0.0
!
! allow one path to eventurally get to alkyl-benzenes 
! and one path to get to consume alkenyl-cyclohexanes
!
!
! Reaction Classes 8 Alkenyl radical decomposition:
!
NBCH-1N3J => C2H4+NC3H7+C5H6-L 2.24E+15 -0.031 30021.0! ring opening. Reverse rate is 1,6 endo addition
                                                           ! based on CHXRAD=>C6H111-6      1.e13 at 1000K.  Falloff needed. 
CHXDCH22N+NC3H7=NBCH-1N3J 8.80E03 2.48 6130.0            ! nbch2n1j is resonant with nbch-1n3j. Addition to one end of an unsubstituted double bond.
                                                           ! analogy to C3H6+C2H5=2-C5H11 Curran IJCK 2006
NBCH-1N3J => C2H4+C2H2+C3H4-A+NC3H7 2.24E+15 -0.031 30021.0 ! ring-opening. nbch2n1j is resonant with nbch-1n3j. 
NBCH-1N3N+H=NBCH-1N3J  1.25E+12 0.51 2620. ! Rules from HJC Table 3 IJCK 38: 250�275 (2006). Allylic Ea reduced by 1000 cal
                                            ! Addition to one end of double bond with one carbon substitution.  nbch1n4j is not included in the mechanism. Only consifer addition to one side of double bond.
NBCH-1N5N+H =NBCH-1N3J 2.50E11 0.51 2620.0 ! nbch2n1j is resonant with nbch-1n3j. Only consider addition to one side of double bond with a carbon substitution.
                                             ! analogy to C3H6+H=n-C3H7 (Curran IJCK 2006, table 3)
! Only consider alkyl-cyclohexadienes:
!nbch2n-an+h=nbch-1n3j 2.50e11 0.51 2620.0 ! addition to one side of a double bond with a carbon substitution
                                             ! analogy to C3H6+H=n-C3H7 (Curran IJCK 2006, table 3)
! ech1n-bn not in mech.  Add this later if it is introduced into the mech:
!c2h5+ech1n-bn=nbch1n-aj 8.80e03 2.48 6130.0 ! Addition to one end of a double bond without carbon substitution.
!                                                ! analogy to C3H6+C2H5=2-C5H11 Curran IJCK 2006
! nbch-1n-aj and nbch-an2j are resonant.  Can ring open from either configuration. Use double ring opening rate:
! Consider two sets of products for ring opening. Assign 1/2 of the total rate to each path: 
NBCH-1N-AJ => C2H4+X135C6H8+C2H5 1.1E+15 -0.031 30020.0 ! do not consider branched diene formed. Use linear diene instead.
                                                           ! ring opening. Reverse rate is 1,6 endo addition
                                                           ! based on CHXRAD=>C6H111-6      1.e13 at 1000K.  Falloff needed. 
NBCH-1N-AJ => C2H4+C6H101-5+C2H3 1.1E+15 -0.031 30020.0  ! ring opening. Reverse rate is 1,6 endo addition
                                                           ! based on CHXRAD=>C6H111-6      1.e13 at 1000K.  Falloff needed. 
! Only including cyclohexadienes:
!h+nbch1n-bn=nbch1n-aj 2.50e11 0.51 2620.0 ! Addition to one end of double bond with one carbon substitution.  nbch1nbj is not included in the mechanism. Only consifer addition to one side of double bond.
                                              ! analogy to C3H6+H=nC3H7 (Curran IJCK 2006, table 3)
!h+nbch2n-an=nbch1n-aj 2.50e11 0.51 2620.0 ! nbch1n-a is resonant with nbch1n-a.  Addition to one end of double bond with one carbon substitution. 
                                              ! analogy to C3H6+H=nC3H7 (Curran IJCK 2006, table 3)
NBCH-1N6J => C2H4+C4H4+PC4H9 2.2E+15 -0.03 30000.0 ! ring opening, one set of products chosen.  Reverse rate is 1,6 endo addition with two double bonds in structure
                                                     !  use 1,6 endo addition with one double bond from CHXRAD=>C6H111-6 
NBCH-1N6J=CYHX14ENE+PC4H9 1.230E+47 -9.740 74260.0! 1,2 cyclohexadiene not included in mech, use 1,4 instead
                                                       ! analogy to ic4h7<=>c3h4-a+ch3 which also forms a 1,2-diene
H+NBCH-1N5N=NBCH-1N6J 2.50E11 0.51 2620.0 ! Addition to one end of double bond with one carbon substitution.
                                             ! analogy to C3H6+H=n-C3H7 (Curran IJCK 2006, table 3)
! Can ring open from either resonant structure:
NBCH-2N4J => X135C6H8+PC4H9 2.2E+15 -0.03 30000.0  ! Ring opening. Bond between C5 and C6 breaks. Reverse rate is 1,6 endo addition with two double bonds in structure  
                                                     !  use 1,6 endo addition with one double bond from CHXRAD=>C6H111-6
                                                     ! Reaction occurs in two steps: make one way. 
NBCH-2N4J => C2H4+2C2H2+PC4H9 1.0E08 0.86 1903.0  ! nbch3n2j resonant with nbch-2n4j. Ring opening.
                                                    ! reverse rate is 1,6 exo addition with 1 double bond in ring formed.
                                                    ! analogy to c7h131-7=cychexch2 with no double bond in cyclic ring formed
CYHX13ENE+PC4H9=NBCH-2N4J    1.70E04 2.48 6130.0 ! nbch3n2j resonant with nbch-2n4j. Addition to carbon substituted double bond.  Degeneracy=2. Tertiary C-C broken. Should be fast. 
                                                    ! analogy to C3H6+C2H5=2-C5H11 Curran IJCK 2006
H+NBCH-2N4N=NBCH-2N4J 2.50E11 0.51 2620.0 ! nbch2n5j is not included in the mechanism. Only consider addition to one side of carbon substituted double bond.
                                            ! analogy to C3H6+H=nC3H7 (Curran IJCK 2006, Table 3)
H+NBCH-1N3N=NBCH-2N4J 6.25E11 0.51 2620.0 ! Note that nbch-2n4j and nbch3n2j are resonant.  Addition to one side of double bond that is DOUBLY carbon substituted.
                                            ! analogy with iC4H8+H=i-C4H9
!nbch-3n5j=x136c7h10+nc3h7 ! Ring opening. x136c7h10 not consumed in mechanism, nor any other c7h10.
NBCH-3N5J => C4H5-N+C6H12-1  5.20E+15 0.058 37521.0     ! Ring opening and then breaks vinyl C-C bond. 2.e7 at 1000K
                                                          ! analogy with MCH3N5J=>X13C7H116.  Reverse rate from fwd using thermo.
                                                          ! did not choose x136c7h10 as a product since it is not consumed in mechanism.
                                                          ! This is a multistep reaction so make it in forward direction only
H+NBCH-2N4N=NBCH-3N5J 2.50E11 0.51 2620.0 ! H addition to one end of a double bond that is carbon substituted.
                                            ! analogy to C3H6+H=nC3H7 (Curran IJCK 2006, Table 3)
NBCH-AN-BJ => 2C2H4+C6H9-A 2.24E+15 -0.031 30020.0 ! Don't have 1,3-c6h9-3 (vinyl radical).  Use x15c6h9-3 (an allylic radical) instead.
                                                       ! ring opening. Reverse rate is 1,6 endo addition
                                                       ! based on CHXRAD=>C6H111-6      1.e13 at 1000K.  Falloff needed. 
! npch-an-bn+ch3=nbch-an-bj ! include this rxn if npch-an-bn in mech
! h+nbch-an-cn=nbch-an-bj ! include this reaction if nbch-an-cn included in mech
!
NBCH-BN-CJ => 2C2H4+C6H9-A 1.0E08 0.86 1903.0  ! reverse ring opening is a 1,6 exo-addition
                                                  ! reverse rate is 1,6 exo addition with no double bonds inside cyclic ring formed
                                                  ! analogy to c7h131-7=cychexch2 
! nbch-bn-dn+h=nbch-bn-cj ! add rxn if nbch-bn-dn added to mech.
CHXRAD+C4H6=NBCH-CN-DJ 1.760E04 2.48 6130 ! secondary radical addition to the terminal end of a double bond. Can add to either end. deg=2.
                                              ! analogy to C3H6+C2H5=2-C5H11
                                              ! H. J. Curran, Int. J. Chem. Kinet. 38 (4) (2006) 250-275.
! h+nbch-bn-cn=nbch-cn-dj ! include if nbch-bn-cn included in mech
!
! Reaction Classes 8b: Alkenyl radical isomerization:
!
! nbch4n3j=nbch2n3j !resonant with nbch3n2j.  1,4 shift allylic to allylic. This looks highly strained due to sp2 structure of double bond and due to resonance. 
!
! Reaction Class 9: Alkene decomposition:
!
! Need to add these!!!!
!
!Consume new species formed by reaction classes
!
! Consume alkylated cyclohexadienes:
!
!nbch1n3n
!
! only consider one radical formed, nbch1n3n5j
! lump nbch1n3n5j, nbch1n3n6j and nbch1n3n-aj into nbch1n3n5j:
! (6 possible secondary allylic Hs to abstract. Also include 2 sec groups and one ch3 group => deg=9
NBCH-1N3N+H    =NBCH1N3N5J+H2     1.52E+06  2.36  2.070E+02
NBCH-1N3N+OH   =NBCH1N3N5J+H2O    1.24E+05  2.64  -1.919E+03
NBCH-1N3N+CH3  =NBCH1N3N5J+CH4    1.66E+01  3.31  4.002E+03
NBCH-1N3N+HO2  =NBCH1N3N5J+H2O2   4.34E+04  2.55  1.053E+04
NBCH-1N3N+O    =NBCH1N3N5J+OH     2.97E+06  2.43  1.210E+03
NBCH-1N3N+O2   =NBCH1N3N5J+HO2    9.90E+12  0.00  3.722E+04
NBCH-1N3N+CH3O =NBCH1N3N5J+CH3OH  1.80E+02  2.90  8.609E+03
NBCH-1N3N+CH3O2=NBCH1N3N5J+CH3O2H 2.17E+04  2.55  1.053E+04
!
!nbch1n5n
!
! only consider one radical formed, nbch1n5n3j
! lump nbch1n5n3j, nbch1n5n4j and nbch1n5n-aj into nbch1n5n3j:
! (6 possible secondary allylic Hs to abstract. Also include 2 sec groups and one ch3 group => deg=9
NBCH-1N5N+H    =NBCH1N5N3J+H2     1.52E+06  2.36  2.070E+02
NBCH-1N5N+OH   =NBCH1N5N3J+H2O    1.24E+05  2.64  -1.919E+03
NBCH-1N5N+CH3  =NBCH1N5N3J+CH4    1.66E+01  3.31  4.002E+03
NBCH-1N5N+HO2  =NBCH1N5N3J+H2O2   4.34E+04  2.55  1.053E+04
NBCH-1N5N+O    =NBCH1N5N3J+OH     2.97E+06  2.43  1.210E+03
NBCH-1N5N+O2   =NBCH1N5N3J+HO2    9.90E+12  0.00  3.722E+04
NBCH-1N5N+CH3O =NBCH1N5N3J+CH3OH  1.80E+02  2.90  8.609E+03
NBCH-1N5N+CH3O2=NBCH1N5N3J+CH3O2H 2.17E+04  2.55  1.053E+04
!
!nbch-2n4n
!
! only consider one radical formed, nbch2n4n3j
! lump nbch2n4n6j, nbch2n4n1j and nbch2n4n-aj into nbch2n4n6j:
! assume secondary allylic rate expresion
! 2 possible secondary allylic Hs and 1 tertiary allylic to abstract. 
! (count tertiary H as 2 because it is about twice as easy to abtract by OH)
! Also include 3 sec groups and one ch3 group => deg=8
NBCH-2N4N+H    =NBCH2N4N6J+H2     1.35E+06  2.36  2.070E+02
NBCH-2N4N+OH   =NBCH2N4N6J+H2O    1.11E+05  2.64  -1.919E+03
NBCH-2N4N+CH3  =NBCH2N4N6J+CH4    1.48E+01  3.31  4.002E+03
NBCH-2N4N+HO2  =NBCH2N4N6J+H2O2   3.86E+04  2.55  1.053E+04
NBCH-2N4N+O    =NBCH2N4N6J+OH     2.64E+06  2.43  1.210E+03
NBCH-2N4N+O2   =NBCH2N4N6J+HO2    8.80E+12  0.00  3.722E+04
NBCH-2N4N+CH3O =NBCH2N4N6J+CH3OH  1.60E+02  2.90  8.609E+03
NBCH-2N4N+CH3O2=NBCH2N4N6J+CH3O2H 1.93E+04  2.55  1.053E+04
!
! ech1n-bn  
! product of nbch1n-aj decomposition. Add later if deemed needed.
! only consider one radical formed, ech1n-bn3j
! lump ech1n-bn3j, and ech1n-bn6j into ech1n-bn3j:
! (4 possible secondary allylic Hs to abstract. Also include 2 sec groups => deg=6
  
! ech1n-bn+h    =ech1n-bn3j+h2      1.01E+06  2.36  2.070E+02  
! ech1n-bn+oh   =ech1n-bn3j+h2o     8.29E+04  2.64  -1.919E+03 
! ech1n-bn+ch3  =ech1n-bn3j+ch4     1.11E+01  3.31  4.002E+03  
! ech1n-bn+ho2  =ech1n-bn3j+h2o2    2.89E+04  2.55  1.053E+04  
! ech1n-bn+o    =ech1n-bn3j+oh      1.98E+06  2.43  1.210E+03  
! ech1n-bn+o2   =ech1n-bn3j+ho2     6.60E+12  0.00  3.722E+04  
! ech1n-bn+ch3o =ech1n-bn3j+ch3oh   1.20E+02  2.90  8.609E+03  
! ech1n-bn+ch3o2=ech1n-bn3j+ch3o2h  1.45E+04  2.55  1.053E+04  
