! Reaction class xx: Consumption of dienes
!
! Low temperature reactions
!
! Reaction Class 13.  R+HO2=RO+OH
!
!
! Reaction Class 9b. alkenoxy decomposition:
! Each alkenyl resonantly stabilized radical forms two types of alkenyloxy radicals. They are lumped into one radical. 
! Some of these rates are very fast are likely in fall-off
CYHX1N3*O+PC4H9=NBCH1N3OJ  2.50E10 0. 10090.0 ! Curran IJCK 2006, Table 12: analogy with: CH3COCH3+CH3=tC4H9O 
!
! The following are alkenoxy decompositions are ring opening reactions.  Little work on these cyclic alkenoxy reactions have been done. 
! The high pressure rate constants of these reactions seem very fast up to 1.0e13 to 1.0e14 at 1000K.  
! Thus these reaction will be in the fall-off.  Assume high pressure rate and assume these radical mainly decompose.
! Use cyclohexenoxy forward rate (cyhx1n3oj=>hx2enal6j) which is from reverse rate and thermo.
!
NBCH1N6OJ => C2H4+NC3H7+C4H6+CO 1.34E+14 0.152 4046.0 ! Do not have product 2-methylenebut-3-enal in mech.  
                                     ! Use reasonable set of other products based on decomposition
                                     ! Analogy to MCH1N6OJ=>BC6H10CHO-AF Rate 5e13 at 1000K.
NBCH2N4OJ=C6H12-1+CH2CHCHCHO 3.53E+13 0.351 6384.0  ! Analogy to cyhx1n3oj=>hx2enal6j 
NBCH3N5OJ=C6H12-1+CH2CHCHCHO  3.53E+13 0.351 6384.0  ! Analogy to cyhx1n3oj=>hx2enal6j 
!
! In the following decompositions, the ring is assumed not to open:
!
NBCH1N-AOJ =CYHX1N4J+NC3H7CHO   5.53E+22 -2.728 22557.0 ! rate is analogy with chxch2oj=>ch2o+chxrad. Should use cyhx1n2j, but not in mech  
NBCH-AN-BOJ=CHXDCH23J+C2H5CHO   5.53E+22 -2.728 22557.0 ! rate is analogy with chxch2oj=>ch2o+chxrad. Should use cyhxdch21j, but not in mech
NBCH-BN-COJ=CHXRAD+AC3H5CHO     5.53E+22 -2.728 22557.0 ! rate is analogy with chxch2oj=>ch2o+chxrad. Do not have but-2-enal in mech so use but-1-enal (ac3h5cho)
CYCHEXCH2+C2H3CHO=NBCH-CN-DOJ  3.33E10 0.0 6397.0 ! Curran IJCK 2006, table 12: analogy with: CH3CHO+C2H5=sC4H9O
!
