NBCH-AJ+CH3O2=NBCH-AOJ+CH3O 7.000E+12  0.00 -1.000E+03
NBCH-BJ+CH3O2=NBCH-BOJ+CH3O 7.000E+12  0.00 -1.000E+03
NBCH-CJ+CH3O2=NBCH-COJ+CH3O 7.000E+12  0.00 -1.000E+03
NBCH-DJ+CH3O2=NBCH-DOJ+CH3O 7.000E+12  0.00 -1.000E+03
!
! Reaction Class 15:  Alkyl peroxy radical isomerization (ROO= QOOH)
! The LLNL 6-membered ring rates are about 10 times slower than Villano et al. rates.  Villano et al. rates will give much higher
! influence of RO2 isomerizations from the ring to the alkyl chain. The Davis et al. rate from the ring to the alkyl chain is consistent with this.
! nbch-1o2:
NBCH-1O2=NBCH-1Q-2J  5.6E-05  4.9 24191.0 ! 5-membered ring. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q2j, 50 bar rate.
                                            ! Reduce rate because the OO group is axial (alkyl group is equilateral)     
                                            ! and the C-H is pointing equilateral.  Reduced by an arbitrary factor of 2
NBCH-1O2=NBCH-1Q-3J  5.66E+02 2.7 21637.0 ! 6-membered ring.  50 atm rate from Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q3j
NBCH-1O2=NBCH-1Q-4J  6.06E+02 2.8 26308.0 ! 7-membered ring. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q4j, 50 bar rate.
! using Sharma et al. rates 2009 as in Bugler et al. 2014:
NBCH-1O2=NBCH-1Q-AJ  6.51E+09 0.70 30100.0 ! 5-membered ring. BC5H11O2<=>BC5H10OOH-C Reaction rate iso-pentane, Bugler et al., 8/29/2014
NBCH-1O2=NBCH-1Q-BJ  7.03E+10 0.20 18500.0 ! 6-membered ring. Reaction rate n-pentane (C5H11O2-2<=>C5H10OOH2-4), Bugler et al., 8/29/2014
                                             ! Don't have a rate for tert to sec from Sharma et al., so used sec to sec.; Tert to sec could be 3 x faster
                                             ! because sec to sec is 3 times faster at 800K than prim to sec (Sharma's rates) 
NBCH-1O2=NBCH-1Q-CJ  3.72E+06 1.20 16600.0 ! 7-membered ring. Reaction rate n-pentane (C5H11O2-1<=>C5H10OOH1-4), Bugler et al., 8/29/2014
NBCH-1O2=NBCH-1Q-DJ  3.90E6   1.0  18200.0 ! 8-membered ring, primary, (1,7s) Sharma et al. JPCA 2010 (not in Bugler et al.)
!
! Sarathy et al. 2011 rate rule:
!nbch-1o2=nbch-1q-aj  2.0e11   0.0 26450.0 ! 5-membered ring. Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011
!nbch-1o2=nbch-1q-bj  2.5e10   0.0 20450.0 ! 6-membered ring. Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011
!nbch-1o2=nbch-1q-cj  3.12e9   0.0 18650.0 ! 7-membered ring. Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011, deg=2
!nbch-1o2=nbch-1q-dj 5.85e8   0.0 25150.0 ! 8-membered ring. Primary C-H, deg=3, Reaction rate rule, primary C-H, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011
!
! nbch-2o2:
!
NBCH-2O2=NBCH-2Q-1J  2.8E-05 4.9 24191.0  ! 5-membered ring. Tert C-H. Deg=1.  Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q2j, 50 bar rate ! 
                                            ! Divide A-factor by 4 compared to chx. Rate is slower because the most favorable position is when
                                            ! OO is axial and the H being pulled off is equilateral.
                                            ! However, rate is faster because C-H is tertiary.  Assume this factor of 2 effect cancels out.
NBCH-2O2=NBCH-2Q-3J  5.6E-05  4.9 24191.0 ! 5-membered ring. Deg=2. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q2j, 50 bar rate ! a-factor /2 - deg=4 in chx.
!
NBCH-2O2=NBCH-2Q-AJ  1.28E6  1.82 16420.0 ! 6-membered ring.  Davis and Pitz, ab intio rate with tunneling and rotor calculations 2012-12 (Weber et al. CF2014)
                                            ! reaction in MCH is: mch2oo=mch2qx
                                            ! Multiply A factor by 2/3 and reduce Ea by 3.3 kcal (101.2-97.9 kcal) for secondary C-H rather than primary C-H
NBCH-2O2=NBCH-2Q-4J  2.83E+02 2.7 21637.0 ! 6-membered ring. Deg=2. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q3j, 50 bar rate ! a-factor/2 since degeneracy is 4 in chx. 
NBCH-2O2=NBCH-2Q-6J  2.83E+02 2.7 21637.0 ! 6-membered ring. Deg=2. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q3j, 50 bar rate ! a-factor/2 since degeneracy is 4 in chx. 
!
NBCH-2O2=NBCH-2Q-5J  6.06E+02 2.8 26308.0 ! 7-membered ring. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q4j, 50 bar rate. 
!
! from Sharma et al. 2010:
! Correct for 1 rotor already "tied up" in the reactant => multiply Afactor by 3?:
NBCH-2O2=NBCH-2Q-BJ  3.72E6 1.2 16600.0 ! 7-membered ring. Sec O-O with Sec C-H abstracted.  Ring to alkyl chain, deg=2
                                          ! analogy to CH3CH2CH2CH2CH2OO -----> CH3CH(.)CH2CH2CH2OOH (1,6s) (prim to sec)
!
!Sarathy et al. 2011:
!nbch-2o2=nbch-2q-bj  3.12e9   0.0 18650.0 ! 7-membered ring. Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011, deg=2
!
! Correct for 1 rotors already "tied up" in the reactant=> multiply Afactor by 3?:
NBCH-2O2=NBCH-2Q-CJ  3.9E8    0.0 21650.0 ! 8-membered ring. Reaction rate rule, sec C-H, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011, deg=2
!
! nbch-3o2:
! Don't lump nbch-3q-2j and nbch-3q-4j as in MCH mech: (seems to selective for lumping)
!nbch-3o2=nbch-3q-2j  1.12E-04 4.9 24191.0  ! 5-membered ring. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q2j, 50 bar rate
NBCH-3O2=NBCH-3Q-2J  5.6E-05 4.9 24191.0  ! 5-membered ring. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q2j, 50 bar rate, a-factor/2 compared to chx 
NBCH-3O2=NBCH-3Q-4J  5.6E-05 4.9 24191.0 ! 5-membered ring. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q2j, 50 bar rate, a-factor/2 compared to chx 
!
NBCH-3O2=NBCH-3Q-1J  1.42E+02 2.7 19637.0  ! 6-membered ring. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q3j, 50 bar rate ! 
                                             ! a-factor /4 - for consistency with chx. Reduce Ea by 1.7 kcal ~ 2 kcal (97.93-96.25) for tertiary C-H instead of secondary,
                                             ! based on reactions rate rules for RH+HO2
NBCH-3O2=NBCH-3Q-5J  2.83E+02 2.7 21637.0 ! 6-membered ring. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q3j, 50 bar rate ! a-factor/2 since degeneracy is 1/2 compared to chx. 
!
NBCH-3O2=NBCH-3Q-6J  6.06E+02 2.8 26308.0 ! 7-membered ring. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q4j, 50 bar rate. 
! Correct for 2 rotors already "tied up" in the reactant => multiply Afactor by 3^2=9?:
!
! from Sharma et al. 2010:
NBCH-3O2=NBCH-3Q-AJ  3.72E6 1.2 16600.0 ! 7-membered ring. Sec O-O with Sec C-H abstracted.  Ring to alkyl chain, deg=2
                                          ! analogy to CH3CH2CH2CH2CH2OO -----> CH3CH(.)CH2CH2CH2OOH (1,6s) (prim to sec)
! Correct for 2 rotors already "tied up" in the reactant => multiply Afactor by 9?:
NBCH-3O2=NBCH-3Q-BJ  2.6E6  1.0 18200.0  ! 8-membered ring. Sec O-O with Sec C-H abstracted.  Ring to alkyl chain, deg=2
                                           ! analogy to CH3CH2(CH2)4OO-->CH3CH(.)(CH2)4OOH(1,7s) (prim to sec)
!Sarathy et al. 2011:
!nbch-3o2=nbch-3q-aj  3.12e9   0.0 18650.0 ! 7-membered ring. Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011, deg=2
!
! Correct for 2 rotors already "tied up" in the reactant => multiply Afactor by 9?:
!nbch-3o2=nbch-3q-bj  3.9e8    0.0 21650.0 ! 8-membered ring. Reaction rate rule, sec C-H, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011, deg=2
!
! nbch-4o2:
NBCH-4O2=NBCH-4Q-3J  1.12E-04 4.9 24191.0 ! 5-membered ring. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q2j, 50 bar rate
NBCH-4O2=NBCH-4Q-2J  5.66E+02 2.7 21637.0 ! 6-membered ring. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q3j, 50 bar rate
NBCH-4O2=NBCH-4Q-1J  3.03E+02 2.8 24308.0 ! 7-membered ring. deg=1. Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chxo2j => chx1q4j, 50 bar rate ! a-factor/2 - for consistency with chx (deg=2). 
                                            ! Ea reduced by 2 kcal for tertiary rather than secondary C-H
!
! from Sharma et al. 2010:
! Correct for 2 rotors already "tied up" in the reactant => multiply Afactor by 3^2=9?:
NBCH-4O2=NBCH-4Q-AJ 2.6E6  1.0  18200.0  ! 8-membered ring. Sec O-O with Sec C-H abstracted.  Ring to alkyl chain, deg=2
                                           ! analogy to CH3CH2(CH2)4OO-->CH3CH(.)(CH2)4OOH(1,7s) (prim to sec)
!
! Sarathy et al. 2011:
! Correct for 2 rotors already "tied up" in the reactant => multiply Afactor by 3^2=9?:
!nbch-4o2=nbch-4q-aj  3.9e8  0.0 21650.0  ! 8-membered ring. Reaction rate rule, sec C-H, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011, deg=2
!
! nbch-ao2:
!
! As in Bugler et al. 2014: (rates are from Sharma et al. 2009)
NBCH-AO2=NBCH-AQ-1J  7.449E+09  0.600 27300.0 !5-membered ring. tert C-H, deg=1, Bugler et al. (CC5H11O2<=>CC5H10OOH-B) from Sharma et al. 2009
NBCH-AO2=NBCH-AQ-BJ  1.716E+09  0.900 29500.0 !5-membered ring. sec C-H, deg=2, Bugler et al. (C5H11O2-2<=>C5H10OOH2-3) from Sharma et al. 2009
NBCH-AO2=NBCH-AQ-CJ  7.033E+10  0.200 18500.0 !6-membered ring. sec C-H, deg=2, Bugler et al. (C5H11O2-2<=>C5H10OOH2-4) from Sharma et al. 2009
NBCH-AO2=NBCH-AQ-DJ  1.233E+06  1.500 20000.0 !7-membered ring. Primary C-H, deg=3, Bugler et al. (C5H11O2-2<=>C5H10OOH2-5) from Sharma et al. 2009 
! Correct for 1 rotor already "tied up" in the reactant => multiply Afactor by 3?:(it looks like a facile RO2 isomerization)
NBCH-AO2=NBCH-AQ-2J  1.41E+11  0.200 18500.0 !6-membered ring. sec C-H, sec O-O, deg=4, Bugler et al. (C5H11O2-2<=>C5H10OOH2-4) 
                                               !from Sharma et al. 2009 analogy to CH3CH2CH2CH(CH3)OO (methyl substitution at OO site => sec O-O)
! Correct for 2 rotors already "tied up" in the reactant => multiply Afactor by 3^2=9?:
NBCH-AO2=NBCH-AQ-3J  7.44E6 1.2 16600.0 ! 7-membered ring. Sec O-O with Sec C-H abstracted.  Ring to alkyl chain, deg=4
                                          ! analogy to CH3CH2CH2CH2CH2OO -----> CH3CH(.)CH2CH2CH2OOH (1,6s) (prim to sec)
!
! Correct for 3 rotors already "tied up" in the reactant => multiply Afactor by 3^3=27?:
NBCH-AO2=NBCH-AQ-4J  2.6E6  1.0  18200.0  ! 8-membered ring. Sec O-O with Sec C-H abstracted.  Ring to alkyl chain, deg=2
                                            ! analogy to CH3CH2(CH2)4OO-->CH3CH(.)(CH2)4OOH(1,7s) (prim to sec)
!
! Sarathy et al. 2011 rules:
!nbch-ao2=nbch-aq-1j  1.00e11 0.0 23700.0 !5-membered ring. tert C-H, deg=1, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011
!nbch-ao2=nbch-aq-bj  2.00e11 0.0 26450.0 !5-membered ring. sec C-H, deg=2, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011
!nbch-ao2=nbch-aq-dj  4.68e9  0.0 21950.0 !7-membered ring. Primary C-H, deg=3, Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011
!
!nbch-ao2=nbch-aq-cj  2.5e10  0.0 20450.0 !6-membered ring. sec C-H, deg=2, Sarathy et al. rule, iso-alkanes, Comb. Flame 2011
