! Reaction Class 22:  RO decomposition
! Unless otherwise noted, rates for ring opening steps are from  MCH mech v9l for mchoj. 
! Rates specified in forward direction are from the reverse addition rate and microscopic reversibility using thermo and the MCH mech) 
!
CHX1*O+PC4H9=NBCH-1OJ          2.92E+03 2.36   8360.0  
NBCH-1OJ => 2C2H4+CH2CO+PC4H9   2.13E19 -1.096 17298.0 ! analogy with mch1oj => ccoccccc
!
NBCH-2OJ => C2H4+CH2CHO+C6H12-1 2.00E+20 -1.332 19899.0
NBCH-2OJ => 2C2H4+C2H3CHO+NC3H7 8.89E+17 -0.817 20344.0
!
NBCH-3OJ => C6H12-1+C3H6CHO-1     1.53E+18 -0.883 20048.0 
NBCH-3OJ => C2H4+AC3H5CHO+PC4H9 7.51E+17 -0.883 20048.0 !partition 1/2 the rate into each of 2 paths
NBCH-3OJ => C2H4+C6H12-1+CH2CHO 7.51E+17 -0.883 20048.0 !partition 1/2 the rate into each of 2 path
!
NBCH-4OJ => C2H4+CH2CHO+C6H12-1   7.51E+17 -0.883 20048.0 !partition 1/2 the rate into each of 2 paths
NBCH-4OJ => C2H4+C4H7CHO-4+NC3H7 7.51E+17 -0.883 20048.0 !partition 1/2 the rate into each of 2 paths
!
CHXRAD+NC3H7CHO=NBCH-AOJ   3.33E10 0.0 5400.0 ! Addition to the carbon on a carbon substituted C=O bond. 
                                                   !From Curran alkoxy radicals IJCK 2006 analogy to CH3CHO+C2H5=sC4H9O. 
                                                   ! Lower Ea by 1 Kcal for secondary radical rather than primary radical (see table 12 in Curran et al.) 
CYCHEXCH2+C2H5CHO=NBCH-BOJ 3.33E10 0.0 6397.0 ! Addition to the carbon on a carbon substituted C=O bond.  
                                                   !From Curran alkoxy radicals IJCK 2006 analogy to CH3CHO+C2H5=sC4H9O. 
!
ECH-BJ+CH3CHO=NBCH-COJ 3.33E10 0.0 6397.0 ! Addition to the carbon on a carbon substituted C=O bond.  
                                                   !From Curran alkoxy radicals IJCK 2006 analogy to CH3CHO+C2H5=sC4H9O. 
!
!
NPCH-CJ+CH2O=NBCH-DOJ 5.00E10 0.0 3457.0 ! Addition of a primary radical to ch2o, analogy CH2O+nC3H7=pC4H9O 
                                             ! From Curran alkoxy radicals IJCK 2006
!
!
! Reaction Class 23:  QOOH=cyclic ether+OH (cyclic ether formation via cyclisation of diradical)
!
! The bicyclics formed could be lumped according to their ring sizes and as to whether the rings are fused or an alkyl chain
! nbch-1q-xj:
! WJP: Oxetan does not form from reactions on the ring because it is too highly strained (Gulati and Walker 1989).  c10-ene-al forms instead.
! c10-ene-al can be branched or straight chain: Lump all these c10-ene-al and assume the molecular structure of dec-5-ene-al
! lump all 1,2 epoxides into one isomer: nbchyo23:
NBCH-1Q-2J=NBCHYO23+OH   8.61E+14 -0.7 13133.0  ! Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chx1q2j => chxyo12+oh, 50 bar rate. nbchyo23 is a lumped species
! two paths to c10-ene-al's:
NBCH-1Q-3J=OH+C10ENE-AL 2.28E+09 0.8 17616.0 ! Fernandes et al. Zador, PCCP 2009 for chx1q3j => hex5enal+oh, 50 bar rate ! 
                                                 ! This is a beta scission path.  The path to the 1,3 epoxide was at or above the entrance channel
                                                 ! and not included.
                                                 ! 1,3 epoxide is unstable and quickly decomposes to C7ene-al (a lumped species) (Gulati and Walker 1989)
                                                 ! However, Lille experimentally observes the 1,3epoxide in the RCM. 
! lump all 1,3 epoxides on the cyclohexane ring into one isomer: nbchyo25:
!nbch-1q-4j=nbchyo25+oh    3.3E+12   0.0   18300.  !added 5.3kcal to form boat form from chair Ea~13kcal
                                                    ! nbchyo25 is a lumped species including mchyo14
NBCH-1Q-4J=NBCHYO25+OH  5.47E+14 -0.7 19426.0 ! Zador 50 bar rate for cyclohexane: chx1q4j => chxyo14+oh. Rate is about 25% slower than above.
!
! reaction rate rule Sarathy et. al. 2011:
! For cyclic ethers on the n-butyl chain, all:
! 3 membered ring cyclic ethers are lumped into nbchyoab
! 4 membered ring cyclic ethers are lumped into nbchyoac
! 5 membered ring cyclic ethers are lumped into nbchyoad
!
! Villano et al. JPCA 2012:
NBCH-1Q-AJ=NBCHYOAB+OH 4.27E+10  0.52   8800.0 ! tert (OOH) - sec (C-H), 3-ring cyclic ether, Bugler et al. 2014 (from Villano et al. 2012) analogy to BC5H10OOH-C<=>B-CC5H10O+OH
