!
! further decomposition paths for gamma mchXqjY
! gamma mchXqjY radical means OOH group is "gamma" to the radical site
! (add these for all gamma mchXqjY if important)=> They are important: 5 times faster at 800K than cyclic ether formation!
! Use to calculate decomposition rate of gamma radical mch2qj4:(mchj2q4ene is c*cccc(c)cjooh):
! mchj2q4ene=mch2qj4   1.00E+08 0.86 5.900E+03 ! A-factor and n from Matheu et al. IJCK 2003 for 1,6 addition to terminal c*c.
! WJP: After talking to Judith Zador, the rate in Fernandez et al. 2007 is a beta scission reaction like the one below. This is a duplicate along
! with others below:
!nbch-1q-3j=oh+c10ene-al 3.8e16 -0.43 27904.2 ! calculated from reverse rate of mchj2q4ene=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
NBCH-1Q-BJ => CHX1*O+C4H8-1+OH  1.182E+20 -2.060 24210.0 !Bugler et al. 2014, analogy with BC5H10OOH-D=>OH+CH3COCH3+C2H4, described as "Not Villano Rates"
!nbch-1q-bj => chx1*o+c4h8-1+oh  1.00e13 0.00 30000.0 ! Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. CnF2011
!nbch-2q-4j=oh+c10ene-al 3.8e16 -0.43 27904.2 ! Gamma QOOH decomp: calculated from reverse rate of c*cccc(c)cjooh=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
!nbch-2q-6j=oh+c10ene-al 3.8e16 -0.43 27904.2 ! Gamma QOOH decomp: calculated from reverse rate of c*cccc(c)cjooh=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
!dup
! WJP: Use slower rate so that radical has time to add to O2:
NBCH-2Q-AJ=OH+C10ENE-AL 2.28E+09 0.8 17616.0 ! Fernandez et al. 2007 for chx1q3j => hex5enal+oh at 50 bar
!nbch-2q-aj=oh+c10ene-al 3.8e16 -0.43 27904.2 ! Gamma QOOH decomp: calculated from reverse rate of c*cccc(c)cjooh=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
!                                                 ! The nbch qooh is a secondary and the MCH qooh is primary, so Ea should be increased.
!nbch-3q-1j=oh+c10ene-al 3.8e16 -0.43 27904.2 ! calculated from reverse rate of mchj2q4ene=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
!nbch-3q-5j=oh+c10ene-al 3.8e16 -0.43 27904.2 ! calculated from reverse rate of mchj2q4ene=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
!dup
!nbch-4q-2j=oh+c10ene-al 3.8e16 -0.43 27904.2 ! Gamma QOOH decomp: calculated from reverse rate of c*cccc(c)cjooh=mch2qj4 using ChemRev
!dup
! WJP: for these QOOH species these are minor paths.  New species were not added for these paths.  Similar species were used.
NBCH-AQ-CJ => C3H6+MCHO+OH     1.180E+09  1.200 22700.0 ! From Bugler et al. 2014 (Villano et al. 2012), analogy with C5H10OOH2-4=>OH+CH3CHO+C3H6, mch-a*o is not in the mech, use isomer mcho (=o on the ring)
!nbch-aq-cj => c3h6+mcho+oh       1.00e13 0.00 30000.0 ! Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. CnF2011.  mch-a*o is not in the mech, use isomer mcho (=o on the ring)
NBCH-AQ-2J => CYCHEXENE+NC3H7CHO+OH 3.530E+09 1.200 21900.0 ! From Bugler et al. 2014 (Villano et al. 2012), analogy with CC5H10OOH-A=>OH+CH3CHO+C3H6
!nbch-aq-2j => cychexene+nc3h7cho+oh 1.00e13 0.00 30000.0 ! Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. CnF2011
NBCH-BQ-1J => CHXDCH2+C2H5CHO+OH 6.270E+08 1.400 23600.0 ! From Bugler et al. 2014 (Villano et al. 2012), analogy with DC5H10OOH-B=>OH+CH2O+IC4H8
!nbch-bq-1j => chxdch2+c2h5cho+oh 1.00e13 0.00 30000.0 ! Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. CnF2011
!nbch-bq-dj=ech-b*o+c2h4+oh 1.00e13 0.00 30000.0 ! Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. CnF2011
NBCH-BQ-DJ => C3H6+MCHO+OH 3.096E+018 -1.730 26820.0 ! From Bugler et al. 2014 (Villano et al. 2012), analogy with C5H10OOH3-1=>OH+C2H5CHO+C2H4 Do not have ech-b*o in mech.  Choose similar products.   
!nbch-bq-dj => c3h6+mcho+oh 1.00e13 0.00 30000.0 ! Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. CnF2011. Do not have ech-b*o in mech.  Choose similar products.   
!nbch-cq-aj=ech-b-ene+ch3cho+oh 1.00e13 0.00 30000.0 ! Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. CnF2011
NBCH-CQ-AJ => CHXDCH2+C2H5CHO+OH 1.180E+09  1.200 22700.0 ! From Bugler et al. 2014 (Villano et al. 2012), analogy with C5H10OOH2-4=>OH+CH3CHO+C3H6 Do not have ech-b-ene. Choose similar products
!nbch-cq-aj => chxdch2+c2h5cho+oh 1.00e13 0.00 30000.0 ! Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. CnF2011.  Do not have npch-c-ene. Choose similar products
!nbch-dq-bj=npch-c-ene+ch2o+oh 1.00e13 0.00 30000.0 ! Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. CnF2011
NBCH-DQ-BJ => CHXDCH2+C2H5CHO+OH 9.100E+08 1.400 25500.0 ! From Bugler et al. 2014 (Villano et al. 2012), analogy with C5H10OOH1-3=>OH+CH2O+C4H8-1 Do not have npch-c-ene. Choose similar products
!nbch-dq-bj => chxdch2+c2h5cho+oh 1.00e13 0.00 30000.0 ! Reaction rate rule, Sarathy et al. CnF2011. Do not have npch-c-ene. Choose similar products
!
