!
! C-H bond breaking: (WJP)
!rxn rate rule for large alkane mechanisms (C5 and C4_53.6 mechs use 3.16e13).
!Use 1.0e14 for H+R=RH. Sarathy et al., Comb. Flame 2011.
DCL-1R+H=DECALIN      1.000E+14       0.00    0.000  
DCL-2R+H=DECALIN      1.000E+14       0.00    0.000  
DCL-3R+H=DECALIN      1.000E+14       0.00    0.000
!
!
!
! Reaction type 2: H-atom abstraction from the fuel
!
! Analogy to rate constants from high-temperature mechanism of MCH (Pitz et al. JPCA 2015)
! Unless otherwise noted, rate constants are from Sarathy, et al., iso-alkanes, Combust. Flame 158 (12) (2011) 2338-2357:
! A-factors from MCH are doubled for degeneracy
! sites in decalin corresponding to sites in MCH:
! decalin-r9 analogy to mchr1
! decalin-r1 analogy to mchr2
! decalin-r2 analogy to mchr3
!
! h rates, uf=2
!
!Use rates for MCH from Wang et al. vol 161 (2014) pp 84�100.  Double A-factor for degeneracy:
!DECALIN+H=DCL-1R+H2     4.06E+06  2.11  4098.6 
!DECALIN+H=DCL-2R+H2     2.16E+07  2.10  6474.4 
!DECALIN+H=DCL-3R+H2     2.14E+07  2.12  6441.2 

DECALIN+H=DCL-1R+H2     9.06E+06  2.11  4098.6 
DECALIN+H=DCL-2R+H2     4.16E+07  2.10  6474.4 
DECALIN+H=DCL-3R+H2     4.14E+07  2.12  6441.2 
!
! rate rule from Sarathy, et al., iso-alkanes, Combust. Flame 158 (12) (2011) 2338-2357:
! Compare to new rates from Chen et al., Computational and Theoretical Chemistry 1026  (2013) 38-45 and from Y. Guan, B. Yang, Chemical Engineering Science 79  (2012) 200-209
DECALIN+CH3=DCL-1R+CH4 1.20E-9  6.362 893.0
DECALIN+CH3=DCL-2R+CH4 6.04     3.46 5481.0
DECALIN+CH3=DCL-3R+CH4 6.04     3.46 5481.0
!
! Reaction with O2, uf=3:
DECALIN+O2=DCL-1R+HO2 2.0E13 0.0 48200.0
DECALIN+O2=DCL-2R+HO2 8.0E13 0.0 49640.0
DECALIN+O2=DCL-3R+HO2 8.0E13 0.0 49640.0
!
! ho2 rates, uf=3                                                                                         
                                                                                                        
! MCH+HO2 rates from Aguilera-Iparraguirre et al. JPCA 2008 for C3 to C4 n-alkanes
DECALIN+HO2=DCL-1R+H2O2     5.24E+02	3.12	11100!1.30E3    3.01  1.209E4  ! WJP: error in exponent in A-factor below  !from IC5H12
DECALIN+HO2=DCL-2R+H2O2     2.53E+02   3.37  1.372E+04 !Healy et al. isobutane, CnF2010.  Similar to Aguilera-Iparraguirre et al. JPCA 2008
DECALIN+HO2=DCL-3R+H2O2     2.53E+02   3.37  1.372E+04 !Healy et al. isobutane, CnF2010
!
! oh rates, uf=2 (uf=uncertainty factor, estimated)
!
! Sivaramakrishnan and J. V. Michael, "Shock tube measurements of high temperature rate constants for 
! OH with cycloalkanes and methylcycloalkanes," Combust. Flame  156 (5) (2009) 1126-1134. 
DECALIN+OH=DCL-1R+H2O         1.02E6 2.06 -1834.0
DECALIN+OH=DCL-2R+H2O         3.90E5 2.451 -1160.0 
DECALIN+OH=DCL-3R+H2O         3.90E5 2.451 -1160.0 
                                                 
DECALIN+CH3O=DCL-1R+CH3OH     4.58E10 0.0 2873.0
DECALIN+CH3O=DCL-2R+CH3OH     5.8E11  0.0 4571.0
DECALIN+CH3O=DCL-3R+CH3OH     5.8E11  0.0 4571.0
