!
! Reaction Class 4. Alkyl radical isomerization
!
! WJP: Because of ring strain, alkylisomerizations on the ring are not expect to occur at a significant rate in the more stable trans-decalin considered here.
! In less-stable cis-decalin, 5-membered alkyl isomerizations may occur based on examiniation of its 3D structure.
!
! Reaction Class 5. H-atom abstraction reactions from alkenes
!
! mch-ac3h5-o (1-allyl-2-methylcyclohexane)
!
! minor product because only formed from fuel decomposition reactionDCYC10H16-1
! Only include paths that have products already in the mechanism
! 2 allylic C-Hs, 2 tertiary C-H, 8 secondary C-Hs, 3 primary C-Hs for 15 total C-Hs
! Assume secondary-H rate with a degeneracy of 16 (Have 15 C-Hs, but some are more or less easily abstracted)
! take from Sarathy et al. Combust. Flame 158 (12) (2011) 2338-2357.
! Distribute among two sets of products already available in the mechanism.  Assume a degeneracy of 8 each to give a total deg=16):
!
NPCHD1A-2M+O2  =>  MCH1ENE+C3H5-A+HO2        8.00E+13 0.00 49640.0
NPCHD1A-2M+OH  =>  MCH1ENE+C3H5-A+H2O        1.87E+08 1.61 -35.0 
NPCHD1A-2M+H  =>  MCH1ENE+C3H5-A+H2          5.20E+06 2.40 4471.0
NPCHD1A-2M+O  =>  MCH1ENE+C3H5-A+OH          2.21E+06 2.45  2830.0
